# Evidence allow-list for results/
#
# The bulk of results/ is large, regenerable research output (full-market
# Wyckoff scans ~1.7 MB each, dated per-symbol analysis dumps) and stays out of
# the repository. What IS tracked is the *structured evidence chain* that backs
# the conclusions published in AGENTS.md / docs/analysis/ — the P-series factor
# studies, the H-A reconciliation, the gate rejections and the data-source
# migration verification.
#
# Every tracked file below is content-hashed in results/EVIDENCE_MANIFEST.json
# and verified in CI by scripts/maintenance/evidence_manifest.py. After an
# intentional evidence change, regenerate the manifest:
#
#     python scripts/maintenance/evidence_manifest.py build
#
# Note: an allow-list here only works because the root .gitignore uses
# `results/*` (not `results/`) — a fully excluded directory cannot re-include.

# 1. Ignore everything directly under results/...
/*
!/.gitignore
!/EVIDENCE_MANIFEST.json

# 2. ...then re-include the curated evidence directories.
!canslim/
!factor_mining/
!h_a_reconcile/
!h_a_signals/
!migration/
!wyckoff_deep_verify/
!wyckoff_experiments/
!wyckoff_verify_20260812/

# 3. ...but keep the multi-megabyte single-run verification dumps out of the
#    repo (regenerable; see scripts/maintenance/ + scripts/factor_mining/).
migration/ashare_all_5000_qfq_verification.json
